1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,003
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:44,043
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,879
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:54,513 --> 00:00:56,055
[panting]

7
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,016
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

8
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:00,519
[grunts, panting]

9
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:05,691
[exhales, panting]

10
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:13,657
[continues panting] Oh, oh...

11
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:17,578
[Isoo continues panting]

12
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:22,582
Kid, go inside.

13
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:23,959
Go inside!

14
00:01:26,295 --> 00:01:27,337
[exhales anxiously]

15
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:30,881
Your heart's pounding.

16
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:32,009
[kid breathing shakily]

17
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:34,344
[♪ music increases in tempo]

18
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:39,473
Drop the knife.
There's nowhere left to run.

19
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,475
Should I kill him?

20
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:44,312
[Pilgu] Drop it.

21
00:01:44,313 --> 00:01:45,938
I'll slice his neck.

22
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,231
[Hyera] Fine.

23
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:48,566
Calm down.

24
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:49,568
[Pilgu] Put it down.

25
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:54,740
Get back.

26
00:01:58,869 --> 00:01:59,911
Drop it.

27
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:01,746
Drop it, you bastards!

28
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:02,956
[kid panting frantically]

29
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:07,585
I said, drop it, you bastards!

30
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:08,753
[taser fires, crackling]

31
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:10,213
[grunting, convulsing]

32
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:16,844
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

33
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,597
[mimics gunshot] You're no big deal.

34
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,726
[grunting]

35
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,895
[siren blaring]

36
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:33,819
[Taegyun] What's going on?
What's the case?

37
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,071
EPISODE 12

38
00:02:35,072 --> 00:02:37,698
This is the real killer
who set Detective Jin up.

39
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:39,159
What are you talking about?

40
00:02:40,744 --> 00:02:42,828
Sir! It's been a while.

41
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:43,996
Wait, he's...

42
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,248
Detective Jin, when did you get out?

43
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:47,417
Yesterday.

44
00:02:48,669 --> 00:02:50,795
I was kind of hurt.

45
00:02:50,796 --> 00:02:52,422
What was it you said to me?

46
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:55,508
[mimicking Taegyun]
"A goddamn detective killed someone?"

47
00:02:55,509 --> 00:02:58,260
How could you say that to me?

48
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:01,055
I liked you, sir, but you've let me down.

49
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:02,640
[Isoo swears softly]

50
00:03:02,641 --> 00:03:04,559
[huffs] Let's go.

51
00:03:06,645 --> 00:03:07,978
[Taegyun] Hey...

52
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:11,983
He won't try to get back at me, will he?

53
00:03:12,401 --> 00:03:16,320
Oh, this is bad, sir.
He doesn't really let things go.

54
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:17,905
I think he'll try to get revenge.

55
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:19,740
This could get really ugly.

56
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,076
Goodness.

57
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:23,203
- Honestly, that punk.
- [♪ music fades]

58
00:03:35,966 --> 00:03:37,383
You did this, didn't you?

59
00:03:37,384 --> 00:03:38,802
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

60
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,681
Kim Younghwan drugged me unconscious...

61
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,268
<i>then let you inside.</i>

62
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,231
What were you two trying to do?

63
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:56,236
Why did you kill Younghwan?

64
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:01,575
We found a bag containing
50 million won inside your house.

65
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:05,703
FORENSIC INVESTIGATION
POLICE

66
00:04:05,704 --> 00:04:07,330
[camera shutter clicking]

67
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:10,792
Where did you get it?

68
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:15,630
[yawns]

69
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:21,428
We found your car, too.

70
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,641
<i>You took the subway from the scene,</i>

71
00:04:28,185 --> 00:04:30,437
<i>then got into your car
at a public parking lot.</i>

72
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:36,734
[camera shutter clicking]

73
00:04:36,735 --> 00:04:38,820
[♪ music swells, fades]

74
00:04:39,488 --> 00:04:41,238
We're investigating it right now.

75
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:42,616
We'll find evidence soon.

76
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:45,285
Just come clean.

77
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:48,872
[clears throat]

78
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:55,796
I want to call my lawyer.

79
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:00,257
I want my phone call.

80
00:05:00,258 --> 00:05:01,968
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

81
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,245
[cell phone vibrating]

82
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:36,962
[cell phone continues vibrating]

83
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,130
[exhales softly]

84
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:42,968
Mr. Lawyer.

85
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:45,428
I've been caught.

86
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:49,098
You're not very skilled.

87
00:05:49,099 --> 00:05:51,226
Of course, I know you well, Mr. Lawyer.

88
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:54,271
I know exactly who you are.

89
00:05:56,064 --> 00:05:57,690
You know me?

90
00:05:57,691 --> 00:05:59,484
You're famous.

91
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:03,864
I'm more thorough than you think.

92
00:06:04,573 --> 00:06:06,366
Then why did you get caught?

93
00:06:07,409 --> 00:06:08,660
Uh...

94
00:06:10,662 --> 00:06:12,497
I was unlucky.

95
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:17,252
In any case,
you'll have to come down here.

96
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,422
I'll send you a lawyer,
so don't say anything.

97
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:23,884
[whispering] You'd better hurry.

98
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:25,844
I'm...

99
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:30,265
not very patient.

100
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:41,985
[♪ music fades]

101
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:44,905
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

102
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,324
GRUDGE, ACCOMPLICE?

103
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:49,951
HOLDS DEEP GRUDGE AGAINST JIN ISOO

104
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:55,498
FOUR STABS TO CHEST, ABDOMEN, BACK

105
00:06:58,376 --> 00:06:59,460
Did you find anything?

106
00:06:59,461 --> 00:07:01,795
There's nothing at the house
but the cash bag.

107
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:04,507
Blood was found on the steering wheel.

108
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,427
They're checking it
against Kim Younghwan's DNA.

109
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:10,096
That's not enough.

110
00:07:12,641 --> 00:07:14,683
You stabbed Kim Younghwan

111
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:17,144
and he went in there to save him.

112
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,354
That makes sense, too.

113
00:07:18,355 --> 00:07:20,314
Isn't there a way to make him confess?

114
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:22,691
He said he won't talk without a lawyer.

115
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:25,445
[scoffs softly] With four convictions,
he knows how this works.

116
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:29,157
But I can't see the bigger picture.

117
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:31,576
Someone gave him that money to do this.

118
00:07:32,661 --> 00:07:33,911
Who could it be?

119
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:36,581
Maybe he was called in to kill you,
then things went wrong.

120
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:40,376
No, that's not what Younghwan said.

121
00:07:40,377 --> 00:07:43,212
What would happen

122
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:46,341
if the great Jin Isoo ended up in prison?

123
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:50,177
He wanted you to get arrested for murder?

124
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:53,723
Like that case where he was the suspect?

125
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,475
Mmm?

126
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:59,229
He was the initial suspect
in the murder of actress Han Yura.

127
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:03,315
<i>He fell asleep after taking drugs,
and there was blood on his clothes.</i>

128
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:04,776
[♪ music increases in tempo]

129
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:10,865
Then,

130
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,826
he ordered Cho Pilgu to kill him?

131
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:15,536
To send Isoo to prison?

132
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:18,331
I don't think anyone would go that far.

133
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:25,296
KIM YOUNGHWAN, CHO PILGU
ACCOMPLICE?

134
00:08:27,465 --> 00:08:29,383
For now, let's look into Cho Pilgu.

135
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:32,052
See if there's a way to make him confess.

136
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:34,304
Did you bring back Cho Pilgu's computer?

137
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:36,056
Yes, Forensics is going through it.

138
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:37,683
[♪ music swells, fades]

139
00:08:37,684 --> 00:08:39,477
[sighs deeply]

140
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:42,772
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

141
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,330
YU SEONGWON
STUDIO

142
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:02,751
[♪ music increases in tempo]

143
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:20,143
YU SEONGWON

144
00:09:25,982 --> 00:09:26,983
[♪ music fades]

145
00:09:29,861 --> 00:09:30,862
[door closes]

146
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:34,782
Are you two sleeping together?

147
00:09:34,783 --> 00:09:35,909
Don't you know how to knock?

148
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:39,036
I wasn't really brought up properly.

149
00:09:39,037 --> 00:09:40,538
At least I got a good show.

150
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:42,624
What do you want?

151
00:09:44,209 --> 00:09:45,752
For you to be a mother for once.

152
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:47,587
Actually,

153
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:51,757
this is more important for you in the end.

154
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:54,928
You know Hansu Group's
Jin Isoo got arrested, right?

155
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:57,514
He was released yesterday.

156
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:00,390
That was my doing.

157
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,102
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

158
00:10:03,061 --> 00:10:04,062
[sighs softly]

159
00:10:05,814 --> 00:10:07,523
4 WEEKS BEFORE KIM YOUNGHWAN'S DEATH

160
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:08,857
Thank you for your time.

161
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:10,568
[Seongwon] Of course. Thank you.
[chuckles softly]

162
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,367
[clears throat]

163
00:10:18,368 --> 00:10:19,661
[Younghwan] Hey, Seongwon.

164
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:22,831
Congratulations.

165
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,461
Hey, I'm hurt.

166
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,630
It's me, Younghwan. Isoo's friend.

167
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:34,634
We met a couple of times before.

168
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,138
Ah.

169
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,681
Right.

170
00:10:40,849 --> 00:10:43,058
- Here.
- Uh, thank you.

171
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:44,309
[chuckles softly]

172
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,645
[♪ music increases in tempo]

173
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,481
Isoo was here yesterday.

174
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,070
Uh... Really?

175
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,071
[chuckles softly] Hey...

176
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:58,366
Anyway, I'm impressed.

177
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,369
You've become such a famous artist.

178
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,495
Even I'm proud of you.

179
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:04,705
[chuckles softly]

180
00:11:04,706 --> 00:11:07,332
How did you make all these amazing pieces?

181
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:08,585
[chuckles]

182
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:11,628
[inhales sharply]

183
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:13,923
Anyway, the thing is,

184
00:11:14,549 --> 00:11:15,925
there's something I want to discuss.

185
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:19,304
Can I visit you at your studio sometime?

186
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:23,558
Of course. Feel free to come.

187
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:26,269
Okay.

188
00:11:27,145 --> 00:11:28,146
I'll call you soon.

189
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,148
Congratulations again.

190
00:11:31,149 --> 00:11:33,026
[♪ ominous, ticking music playing]

191
00:11:35,737 --> 00:11:36,863
[scoffs softly]

192
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:41,450
He's like a dog without its master.

193
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:42,619
[♪ music swells, fades]

194
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:47,623
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

195
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:49,000
[exhales contentedly]

196
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:51,794
[exhales] Even the whiskey you drink
is good.

197
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:54,714
This is the one Isoo made.

198
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:56,257
Never tried it before?

199
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:01,804
Uh... [chuckles nervously]

200
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:04,181
No. [scoffs]

201
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,183
[scoffs softly]

202
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:08,602
Anyway... [sighs]

203
00:12:08,603 --> 00:12:12,648
...shouldn't you start thinking about
selling your pieces now?

204
00:12:12,649 --> 00:12:13,775
Mmm.

205
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:17,153
The thing is,

206
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:23,534
I'm well-connected with
chaebols, celebrities, and big spenders.

207
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,747
People are already lining up
to buy your work.

208
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:30,290
Really?

209
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:33,043
You have no idea.
Right now, they keep calling me

210
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:36,172
to ask if they can buy your work.
[chuckling]

211
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:37,840
So, how about it?

212
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:42,804
Should I take this chance
and become your art dealer?

213
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:47,015
Uh, don't get me wrong. [chuckles]

214
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,978
I'm not trying to use this
to make money or anything like that.

215
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:52,480
Your work is just too good.

216
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:54,857
You run a production company.

217
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:57,402
[chuckles nervously]

218
00:12:58,194 --> 00:12:59,696
Yeah, well,

219
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,823
I'm thinking of quitting.

220
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,867
So the rumors were true.

221
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:06,703
Mmm?

222
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:09,831
I heard you went to prison
for doing drugs.

223
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:17,130
- [sighs wearily]
- Why didn't Isoo help you back then?

224
00:13:17,839 --> 00:13:19,215
Is that why you two fell out?

225
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,052
No.

226
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:26,972
That bastard turned me in.

227
00:13:26,973 --> 00:13:28,849
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

228
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:30,309
Uh...

229
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:31,477
Isoo did that?

230
00:13:32,437 --> 00:13:35,023
Yeah. He was supposed to be my friend.

231
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,523
Uh...

232
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,607
But why?

233
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:40,737
He thinks he's a detective now. [scoffs]

234
00:13:42,572 --> 00:13:47,451
Isoo thinks of himself as a detective?

235
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:50,288
That's why he sold out his own friend.

236
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,292
Are you just going to take that?

237
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:57,252
Actually, I was so pissed off,

238
00:13:57,253 --> 00:14:00,673
I snuck into his house
and thought about killing him.

239
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:02,550
You snuck in?

240
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,345
I have a key to his house.

241
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,808
How about we mess with Isoo a little?

242
00:14:11,726 --> 00:14:12,809
How?

243
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,270
[♪ music turns ominous]

244
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:17,273
Let's get him locked up for drugs, too.

245
00:14:17,899 --> 00:14:20,567
You go inside
and make him take drugs somehow,

246
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:22,486
then I'll send someone.

247
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:25,656
He'll put Isoo in a car
and make him cause an accident.

248
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:29,451
I think it could become a huge scandal.

249
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:30,911
[laughs maliciously]

250
00:14:30,912 --> 00:14:32,371
It's going to be so much fun.

251
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,415
[chuckles nervously]

252
00:14:35,917 --> 00:14:37,000
Uh...

253
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,877
Aren't you close with Isoo?

254
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:40,087
Why would you do that?

255
00:14:40,088 --> 00:14:42,423
He kind of screwed me over.

256
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:47,302
It's fine. It's just a joke.

257
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:50,180
Isoo will be able to get out of it anyway.

258
00:14:50,181 --> 00:14:51,516
And you can just move abroad,

259
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,309
as my art dealer.

260
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:58,396
[chuckles nervously]

261
00:14:58,397 --> 00:14:59,857
[♪ music increases in tempo]

262
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:09,283
Find someone.

263
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:11,785
I need a job done.

264
00:15:11,786 --> 00:15:12,870
Understood.

265
00:15:14,497 --> 00:15:16,790
Are you saying
you gave the order to kill him?

266
00:15:16,791 --> 00:15:18,917
- Yes.
- Why?

267
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:20,001
[♪ music fades]

268
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:22,004
Just because. I thought it'd be fun.

269
00:15:23,131 --> 00:15:24,173
[scoffs]

270
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:27,300
[breathes deeply]

271
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:28,302
But

272
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:31,138
I think he found out who I am.

273
00:15:31,139 --> 00:15:32,472
[♪ tense music playing]

274
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:35,183
How? You said Mr. Hwang hired him.

275
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:36,268
Yeah.

276
00:15:36,269 --> 00:15:37,770
Mr. Hwang dropped off the money.

277
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,231
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

278
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:42,441
[keypad beeping]

279
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:01,544
<i>He must've followed him.</i>

280
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:19,228
[♪ music turns ominous]

281
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:21,939
You...

282
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,234
Why do you...

283
00:16:27,028 --> 00:16:28,862
keep doing this?

284
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:31,073
It's a bit too late to ask that.

285
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:35,369
You should've asked when I was nine,
before you had me committed.

286
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:44,795
You might...

287
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:48,089
want to hurry.

288
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:49,842
If he decides to talk,

289
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,178
me,

290
00:16:52,762 --> 00:16:53,845
you,

291
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,848
and this company you love so much

292
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,018
will be over.

293
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,444
[door opens]

294
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:10,738
[door slams]

295
00:17:12,323 --> 00:17:13,406
[clink]

296
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,617
[screams in frustration]

297
00:17:15,618 --> 00:17:17,327
[breathing heavily]

298
00:17:17,328 --> 00:17:18,412
[sighs in exasperation]

299
00:17:19,914 --> 00:17:21,749
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

300
00:17:46,274 --> 00:17:47,483
[♪ music fades]

301
00:17:50,361 --> 00:17:52,947
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

302
00:17:57,952 --> 00:17:59,120
I'm Mr. Cho Pilgu's lawyer.

303
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:02,373
Okay.

304
00:18:04,584 --> 00:18:05,793
[sighs in exasperation]

305
00:18:07,962 --> 00:18:09,838
Song Yeonwoo.

306
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:12,841
First, please tell me what happened.

307
00:18:12,842 --> 00:18:14,509
[breathes deeply]

308
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:17,178
There's nothing much to tell.

309
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:18,263
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

310
00:18:18,264 --> 00:18:20,891
He opened the door for me, so I went in.

311
00:18:23,769 --> 00:18:25,563
You'll handle the rest, right?

312
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:28,941
I'll leave you to it.

313
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,027
[chuckles]

314
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:33,278
Wait.

315
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:34,404
What?

316
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:36,364
That's not what I was told.

317
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,575
What do you mean?

318
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:39,160
- [squelch]
- [Younghwan grunts softly]

319
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,162
- [squelch]
- [groans]

320
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:42,913
- [squelch]
- [exclaims]

321
00:18:43,331 --> 00:18:45,248
- [groaning]
- [squelching]

322
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:46,416
[exclaims]

323
00:18:46,417 --> 00:18:48,127
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

324
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:50,295
Come here.

325
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:51,714
- [squelch]
- [groans]

326
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:07,313
[exhales softly]

327
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:09,899
[knife clatters]

328
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:13,860
[Pilgu grunts]

329
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:15,404
[♪ music increases in tempo]

330
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:17,448
[grunts]

331
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,245
[grunts]

332
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:26,915
[grunts]

333
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:28,416
[panting]

334
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,794
[♪ music swells]

335
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:32,213
[grunts]

336
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:35,048
[grunts] He's even heavier.

337
00:19:35,049 --> 00:19:36,299
[♪ music resumes tempo]

338
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,301
Any fingerprints?

339
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:40,471
I was wearing gloves the whole time.

340
00:19:41,764 --> 00:19:42,890
We can build a story.

341
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:46,310
The police don't have
any conclusive evidence.

342
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:50,355
We'll say Kim Younghwan took you there
as his bodyguard.

343
00:19:50,356 --> 00:19:52,649
He was afraid Jin Isoo would kill him.

344
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:55,111
You went up there
because he called you for help.

345
00:19:55,945 --> 00:19:57,196
That's how you got blood on you.

346
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,493
We might be here a while.

347
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,412
Why don't we eat something?

348
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,038
[chuckles softly]

349
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,374
- Sounds good.
- [♪ music fades]

350
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,002
[slurps]

351
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:14,921
Just stick to what we rehearsed.

352
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:16,507
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

353
00:20:18,718 --> 00:20:19,719
And sign this.

354
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:23,680
It's a retainer agreement.

355
00:20:23,681 --> 00:20:24,806
[sighs deeply]

356
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:26,308
Such a hassle.

357
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:38,904
[slurps]

358
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:42,950
Expensive lawyers

359
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:45,577
are worth it.

360
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:47,078
Of course.

361
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,163
[chuckles smugly]

362
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:49,415
[slurping]

363
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:53,544
Eat up.

364
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:56,797
[slurping]

365
00:20:59,884 --> 00:21:02,719
INTERVIEW ROOM

366
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:03,721
[♪ music fades]

367
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:12,188
They probably worked out a story.

368
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,651
Without more evidence,
we need to set Cho Pilgu free.

369
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:21,363
[sighs heavily]

370
00:21:23,324 --> 00:21:24,407
Did you find anything?

371
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:27,453
His computer records came back,
but there was nothing significant.

372
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,331
Nothing on his phone either.

373
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,041
Let me see.

374
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:36,462
DIGITAL FORENSIC REPORT

375
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:43,259
YU SEONGWON

376
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,552
What's this?

377
00:21:44,553 --> 00:21:46,514
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

378
00:21:47,515 --> 00:21:50,017
He searched for Yu Seongwon online.

379
00:21:58,442 --> 00:21:59,735
[Isoo] It's Yu Seongwon's studio.

380
00:22:02,488 --> 00:22:04,489
Minjae installed another camera. Let's go.

381
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:05,865
Okay.

382
00:22:05,866 --> 00:22:07,284
[♪ music increases in tempo]

383
00:22:10,204 --> 00:22:11,663
Look up Yu Seongwon.

384
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:12,748
Okay.

385
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:15,250
Did you hear anything about this?

386
00:22:15,251 --> 00:22:16,252
No, nothing.

387
00:22:20,214 --> 00:22:21,382
[line ringing]

388
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:25,636
[automated voice]
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

389
00:22:26,095 --> 00:22:28,137
- [line disconnects]
- He's not picking up.

390
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:29,473
[♪ music swells]

391
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:33,060
[sighs softly]

392
00:22:34,144 --> 00:22:35,603
- [cell phone vibrates]
- [♪ music fades]

393
00:22:35,604 --> 00:22:37,230
PI JEONG MINJAE

394
00:22:37,231 --> 00:22:39,650
[Minjae] <i>I can't pick up right now.
What is it?</i>

395
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:46,407
[Hyera] <i>Did anything happen
with Yu Seongwon yesterday?</i>

396
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,954
[Minjae] <i>He just went back to his studio.</i>

397
00:22:53,289 --> 00:22:54,290
[Hyera] <i>Where are you?</i>

398
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:59,503
[Minjae] <i>I'm staking out
for a different case.</i>

399
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:02,131
[breathes deeply]

400
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,968
Does Yu Seongwon know Kim Younghwan?

401
00:23:06,969 --> 00:23:07,970
Yeah.

402
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:10,598
He met him a few times with me.

403
00:23:11,432 --> 00:23:12,474
But why?

404
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:15,895
I get why Younghwan
would want to get back at me,

405
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:19,440
but what does Seongwon
have to do with this?

406
00:23:22,985 --> 00:23:24,069
[♪ music swells, fades]

407
00:23:27,948 --> 00:23:29,324
Do you know the passcode?

408
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:32,243
Yeah, we know each other's,
just to be safe.

409
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,454
[digital beeping]

410
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:40,878
[sighs softly]

411
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:44,339
That's the monitor for Yu Seongwon.

412
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:45,673
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

413
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:48,594
- Let's check the saved files first.
- Okay.

414
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:52,973
[mouse clicking]

415
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:13,869
[Isoo] Oh.

416
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:15,579
That's Kim Younghwan.

417
00:24:21,168 --> 00:24:22,336
[doorbell chiming]

418
00:24:25,214 --> 00:24:27,256
Did they plan this together?

419
00:24:27,257 --> 00:24:29,927
Yu Seongwon might have
wanted revenge on you.

420
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:33,262
He knows now that you suspect him.

421
00:24:33,263 --> 00:24:35,307
He tried to frame me for murder
because of that?

422
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:37,184
Does that mean

423
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:40,396
Younghwan told Seongwon to murder him?

424
00:24:41,897 --> 00:24:45,316
No, Kim Younghwan was
probably used as well.

425
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:48,861
Cho Pilgu went to Yu Seongwon's studio,

426
00:24:48,862 --> 00:24:50,489
so Yu Seongwon must have hired him.

427
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,741
The 50 million won was
payment for the murder.

428
00:24:53,742 --> 00:24:54,826
[♪ music fades]

429
00:24:54,827 --> 00:24:57,329
Kim Younghwan's plan was something else,

430
00:24:58,539 --> 00:25:01,749
but Yu Seongwon hired someone
to kill Kim Younghwan?

431
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,418
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

432
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:06,130
[Seongwon] <i>I had a feeling
this day would come.</i>

433
00:25:06,797 --> 00:25:09,049
From the first day I met you.

434
00:25:10,384 --> 00:25:11,593
Think back carefully.

435
00:25:12,428 --> 00:25:16,015
Remember how good it felt
when you stabbed Younghwan.

436
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:17,890
[bang]

437
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:19,434
Don't run away from this.

438
00:25:19,435 --> 00:25:22,771
Once you accept it,
you'll finally be free.

439
00:25:24,398 --> 00:25:28,193
After all, you're my Little Prince.

440
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:31,238
It was to awaken me.

441
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:36,285
Yu Seongwon thinks I'm just like him.

442
00:25:37,161 --> 00:25:38,162
That I'm

443
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:40,789
suppressing the urge to kill.

444
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:45,418
So he wanted to turn me
into a murderer like him.

445
00:25:45,419 --> 00:25:46,920
[♪ music increases in tempo]

446
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:50,132
[scoffs]

447
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:51,883
[♪ music resumes tempo]

448
00:25:51,884 --> 00:25:53,343
[grunts, groans]

449
00:25:55,512 --> 00:25:56,638
[keyboard clacking]

450
00:25:58,348 --> 00:26:00,142
[grunting, coughs]

451
00:26:01,977 --> 00:26:03,102
Son of a...

452
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:05,147
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

453
00:26:06,607 --> 00:26:07,733
[keys jingling]

454
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:09,860
[latch clanks]

455
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:15,740
- [touch-tones beeping]
- [guard] A detainee collapsed.

456
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,283
Please call an ambulance.

457
00:26:17,284 --> 00:26:18,952
[grunts, choking]

458
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:21,496
Cho Pilgu collapsed!

459
00:26:21,497 --> 00:26:23,248
[♪ music swells]

460
00:26:29,671 --> 00:26:30,755
[♪ music fades]

461
00:26:30,756 --> 00:26:32,965
- [siren blaring]
- [camera shutters clicking]

462
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,635
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

463
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:42,684
What happened?

464
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:45,354
It's an acute drug overdose.

465
00:26:48,357 --> 00:26:49,941
That lawyer who came earlier.

466
00:26:49,942 --> 00:26:51,610
I'm Mr. Cho Pilgu's lawyer.

467
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:55,405
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

468
00:26:59,493 --> 00:27:00,536
[tires screech]

469
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:05,582
[♪ music swells]

470
00:27:11,421 --> 00:27:12,673
ATTORNEY SONG YEONWOO

471
00:27:13,715 --> 00:27:15,424
[♪ music resumes tempo]

472
00:27:15,425 --> 00:27:17,093
How can I help you?

473
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:19,512
Are you Attorney Song Yeonwoo?

474
00:27:19,513 --> 00:27:22,515
Yes, I'm Song Yeonwoo.

475
00:27:22,516 --> 00:27:23,600
[sighs heavily]

476
00:27:24,226 --> 00:27:25,561
[sighs softly]

477
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:28,355
[Junyoung sighs heavily]

478
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:32,693
He's been dealt with.

479
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:35,028
They won't find out who I am,

480
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:37,531
but I'll lie low for now.

481
00:27:38,532 --> 00:27:39,783
You should delete me

482
00:27:41,118 --> 00:27:42,286
from the company's records.

483
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:56,633
Well done.

484
00:27:57,301 --> 00:27:58,552
[♪ music swells]

485
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:05,601
[♪ music fades]

486
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:11,230
[breathes deeply]

487
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:12,232
[sighs softly]

488
00:28:18,113 --> 00:28:19,906
[Byungsik sighs wearily]

489
00:28:19,907 --> 00:28:21,325
This doesn't look good.

490
00:28:22,993 --> 00:28:23,994
How did this happen?

491
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:27,122
A suspect dying in police custody?

492
00:28:28,457 --> 00:28:31,667
It looks like someone impersonated
a lawyer and drugged him.

493
00:28:31,668 --> 00:28:34,129
Who? Did you find out who it was?

494
00:28:34,755 --> 00:28:36,506
- No, not yet.
- Hey!

495
00:28:37,132 --> 00:28:38,758
Are you trying to ruin me?

496
00:28:38,759 --> 00:28:40,301
You idiots!

497
00:28:40,302 --> 00:28:43,763
After all your fooling around,
this is what you come back with?

498
00:28:43,764 --> 00:28:46,432
Who's going to answer for this?

499
00:28:46,433 --> 00:28:47,726
Tell me, who?

500
00:28:50,395 --> 00:28:53,023
- We'll make sure--
- Hey! You're seriously...

501
00:28:53,607 --> 00:28:54,815
You.

502
00:28:54,816 --> 00:28:56,485
You caused all of this.

503
00:28:57,069 --> 00:28:58,694
Try to say another word.

504
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:01,448
I'll fire you on the spot!

505
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:03,325
Goddamn it!

506
00:29:03,951 --> 00:29:05,076
[grunts angrily]

507
00:29:05,077 --> 00:29:06,495
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

508
00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:10,749
[camera shutter clicking]

509
00:29:11,333 --> 00:29:12,334
[sighs softly]

510
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:17,421
The incident at Detective Jin Isoo's--

511
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:19,800
Is it true that the suspect
of this case has died?

512
00:29:20,634 --> 00:29:22,051
Yes, it's true.

513
00:29:22,052 --> 00:29:24,053
How did they die in police custody?

514
00:29:24,054 --> 00:29:27,348
We're still investigating that matter.

515
00:29:27,349 --> 00:29:30,434
Is it true that the killer impersonated
a lawyer and poisoned him?

516
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:31,728
[reporters clamoring]

517
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:43,031
[♪ music swells]

518
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:54,041
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

519
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:55,127
[♪ music fades]

520
00:30:02,676 --> 00:30:03,677
[exhales heavily]

521
00:30:04,386 --> 00:30:06,555
I'm starving. Let's get something to eat.

522
00:30:08,890 --> 00:30:12,935
Let's eat, then think about
how we'll catch Yu Seongwon.

523
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:14,770
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

524
00:30:14,771 --> 00:30:16,606
This might be an opportunity.

525
00:30:18,025 --> 00:30:20,527
If we can prove
Yu Seongwon orchestrated the murder,

526
00:30:21,445 --> 00:30:24,364
we can catch him
before he kills anyone else.

527
00:30:26,116 --> 00:30:28,160
Yu Seongwon went to UBS's main office.

528
00:30:29,578 --> 00:30:32,205
Minjae was following him
the day before Cho Pilgu died.

529
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:38,462
Maybe he met Jeong Taeseon that day
and asked for her help.

530
00:30:39,755 --> 00:30:42,006
And Jeong Taeseon pulled something?

531
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:43,175
Yes.

532
00:30:43,759 --> 00:30:47,220
[inhales sharply] There wasn't much time,
so it could be someone close to her.

533
00:30:49,264 --> 00:30:50,307
[sighs heavily]

534
00:30:52,142 --> 00:30:54,310
[line connects, ringing]

535
00:30:54,311 --> 00:30:55,644
[automated voice]
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

536
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:57,438
[sighs in exasperation]
Why won't he answer his phone?

537
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:58,564
[line disconnects]

538
00:30:58,565 --> 00:31:00,232
[♪ music swells]

539
00:31:00,233 --> 00:31:01,359
[sighs heavily]

540
00:31:03,361 --> 00:31:04,570
[♪ music fades]

541
00:31:04,571 --> 00:31:05,697
Ms. Joo Hyera?

542
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:07,741
Yes?

543
00:31:17,918 --> 00:31:20,086
[delivery agent]
We have a delivery for you.

544
00:31:20,087 --> 00:31:21,838
[delivery agents grunting]

545
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:25,675
[delivery agent dusts hands]

546
00:31:29,221 --> 00:31:31,264
GANGHA POLICE STATION
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA

547
00:31:34,059 --> 00:31:35,185
[door opens]

548
00:31:37,479 --> 00:31:39,605
- What's that?
- Pass me a box cutter.

549
00:31:39,606 --> 00:31:40,649
[door closes]

550
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:43,568
- [box cutter clicking]
- [tape slicing, ripping]

551
00:31:50,659 --> 00:31:52,077
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

552
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:03,046
[♪ suspenseful sting plays]

553
00:32:07,259 --> 00:32:08,301
[gasps softly]

554
00:32:09,678 --> 00:32:11,178
[Hyera exhales in disbelief]

555
00:32:11,179 --> 00:32:12,263
[whimpers]

556
00:32:12,264 --> 00:32:14,431
[breath trembling]

557
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:15,891
Stop those delivery guys.

558
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:17,144
Got it.

559
00:32:18,645 --> 00:32:19,979
[gasps, sobbing]

560
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:21,273
[♪ music swells]

561
00:32:26,236 --> 00:32:27,237
Min...

562
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:31,867
[♪ music fades]

563
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:35,912
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

564
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:39,291
[camera shutter clicking]

565
00:33:00,020 --> 00:33:01,979
[♪ music swells, fades]

566
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,564
There was a body inside?

567
00:33:03,565 --> 00:33:05,150
We really don't know anything.

568
00:33:06,109 --> 00:33:07,568
Where did you get it from?

569
00:33:07,569 --> 00:33:09,528
[stutters] Namgye-dong.

570
00:33:09,529 --> 00:33:12,114
But that place is a redevelopment area,

571
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:14,074
so everything's been cleared out.

572
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:16,202
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

573
00:33:16,203 --> 00:33:18,622
<i>We were asked to move
something they left behind.</i>

574
00:33:19,247 --> 00:33:21,166
<i>They said the money was on top of the box.</i>

575
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,668
[gasps] Jesus Christ.

576
00:33:26,046 --> 00:33:27,964
So you don't know
who commissioned the job?

577
00:33:28,590 --> 00:33:30,425
We did get a call,

578
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:34,387
but when I tried the number just now,
the phone was off.

579
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:36,014
You don't know their name?

580
00:33:36,556 --> 00:33:37,557
No.

581
00:33:38,308 --> 00:33:39,851
We didn't catch the name.

582
00:33:41,686 --> 00:33:44,356
You transported something
without knowing who hired you?

583
00:33:45,273 --> 00:33:47,108
We've barely had any work recently.

584
00:33:49,236 --> 00:33:51,905
And two million won is a lot of money.

585
00:33:56,034 --> 00:33:57,035
[sighs softly]

586
00:33:58,995 --> 00:34:01,205
[breathing heavily] You damn fool!

587
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:02,665
What the hell happened?

588
00:34:02,666 --> 00:34:04,250
How did we get a body delivered?

589
00:34:04,251 --> 00:34:05,752
You're all out of your damn minds!

590
00:34:06,419 --> 00:34:08,213
Joo Hyera. Where the hell is Joo Hyera?

591
00:34:10,257 --> 00:34:11,548
Let go of me!

592
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:13,509
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

593
00:34:13,510 --> 00:34:15,178
[Taegyun panting softly]

594
00:34:18,348 --> 00:34:19,599
Sir. [sighs softly]

595
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:21,559
For now,

596
00:34:22,894 --> 00:34:23,978
please just stay put.

597
00:34:23,979 --> 00:34:25,230
What?

598
00:34:25,814 --> 00:34:26,856
The person who died

599
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:29,526
was Joo Hyera's junior officer.

600
00:34:30,944 --> 00:34:32,612
He used to work for me, too.

601
00:34:33,405 --> 00:34:34,613
[sighs softly]

602
00:34:34,614 --> 00:34:37,617
I'll face disciplinary action,
or even resign if I have to,

603
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:39,911
so for now,

604
00:34:41,496 --> 00:34:42,914
please don't say anything.

605
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:47,669
Please.

606
00:34:48,461 --> 00:34:49,713
[Taegyun sighs softly]

607
00:34:52,716 --> 00:34:54,466
[sniffles, crying]

608
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:55,593
[sighs deeply]

609
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:01,433
[gasps softly, breath trembling]

610
00:35:03,018 --> 00:35:04,102
[sighs deeply]

611
00:35:05,604 --> 00:35:06,730
[exhales heavily]

612
00:35:16,156 --> 00:35:17,157
[Changun] So it was Minjae.

613
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:21,202
Was Minjae the one

614
00:35:22,329 --> 00:35:23,913
keeping an eye on Yu Seongwon?

615
00:35:26,166 --> 00:35:27,375
[voice shaking] Minjae was

616
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:29,961
following Yu Seongwon.

617
00:35:32,255 --> 00:35:33,798
I lost contact with him after that.

618
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:38,887
I didn't think anything of it.

619
00:35:40,555 --> 00:35:42,057
[breath trembling]

620
00:35:43,016 --> 00:35:44,351
[crying] I just waited.

621
00:35:48,188 --> 00:35:50,231
[gasps softly, breath trembling]

622
00:35:54,778 --> 00:35:55,904
[sighs deeply]

623
00:35:58,031 --> 00:35:59,199
[sniffles]

624
00:35:59,866 --> 00:36:00,867
[voice shaking] Did they find anything?

625
00:36:02,911 --> 00:36:04,204
Not yet.

626
00:36:06,206 --> 00:36:07,666
Let's give it some time.

627
00:36:08,541 --> 00:36:11,418
If we search thoroughly,
I'm sure we'll find something.

628
00:36:11,419 --> 00:36:12,587
No.

629
00:36:14,506 --> 00:36:15,882
We won't find anything.

630
00:36:17,801 --> 00:36:18,927
You know.

631
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:22,347
You know what Yu Seongwon is like.

632
00:36:29,354 --> 00:36:30,355
Hyera.

633
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:32,648
Hey, Joo Hyera.

634
00:36:32,649 --> 00:36:33,817
[♪ music fades]

635
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:38,195
Did you find anything of note?

636
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:40,532
[KCSI officer] Nothing in particular.
We'll go upstairs and check.

637
00:36:41,116 --> 00:36:42,533
[engine accelerating]

638
00:36:42,534 --> 00:36:44,119
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

639
00:36:51,334 --> 00:36:52,377
[Isoo] How did it go?

640
00:36:52,961 --> 00:36:56,464
The truck doesn't seem related.
Forensics didn't find anything.

641
00:36:57,966 --> 00:36:59,968
[sighs in exasperation]
How on earth did this happen?

642
00:37:00,593 --> 00:37:02,094
And who's the person who died?

643
00:37:02,095 --> 00:37:03,847
His name is Jeong Minjae.

644
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:05,681
Detective Joo's old colleague.

645
00:37:05,682 --> 00:37:06,974
What?

646
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:08,560
What colleague...

647
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:11,438
You mean he's a police officer?

648
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:13,565
Not anymore.

649
00:37:14,691 --> 00:37:17,819
They picked up the box from here,
so go with Forensics to check it out.

650
00:37:18,570 --> 00:37:19,696
Okay.

651
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:22,657
Where's Detective Joo?

652
00:37:23,867 --> 00:37:25,118
She left in a hurry earlier.

653
00:37:26,494 --> 00:37:28,037
[♪ music increases in tempo]

654
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:36,379
[engine accelerating]

655
00:37:40,216 --> 00:37:41,384
[♪ music fades]

656
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:46,848
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

657
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:49,350
[footsteps approaching]

658
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:01,112
- [loud, distant bang]
- [alarm blaring]

659
00:38:03,239 --> 00:38:04,699
[gate whirring]

660
00:38:08,411 --> 00:38:09,537
[engine revs]

661
00:38:12,081 --> 00:38:13,291
We have a guest.

662
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,083
Go and see.

663
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:17,170
[♪ foreboding, pulsating music playing]

664
00:38:25,678 --> 00:38:27,055
Yu Seongwon is inside, isn't he?

665
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:40,025
Detective Joo Hyera.

666
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:41,360
Long time no see.

667
00:38:41,361 --> 00:38:42,779
Why did you kill him?

668
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:44,572
What?

669
00:38:45,365 --> 00:38:46,866
Why did you kill him?

670
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:49,327
Hey!

671
00:38:49,994 --> 00:38:50,995
Let go.

672
00:38:55,083 --> 00:38:57,877
Leave. She's my guest.

673
00:39:03,091 --> 00:39:06,094
I'm so sorry. He doesn't have any manners.
[chuckles]

674
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:08,388
Anyway,

675
00:39:09,472 --> 00:39:10,764
did someone die?

676
00:39:10,765 --> 00:39:11,850
[♪ music swells]

677
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:15,478
[♪ music fades]

678
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:19,566
You think you're perfect, don't you?

679
00:39:20,191 --> 00:39:21,733
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

680
00:39:21,734 --> 00:39:23,278
You think after killing five people,

681
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:26,239
you didn't leave
a single trace, don't you?

682
00:39:27,240 --> 00:39:28,283
[scoffs]

683
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:31,160
But you left a long trail this time.

684
00:39:32,078 --> 00:39:33,955
You moved the body,

685
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:35,832
called a truck,

686
00:39:37,083 --> 00:39:38,418
and sent it to me.

687
00:39:40,879 --> 00:39:42,130
Why did you go that far?

688
00:39:44,716 --> 00:39:46,009
Am I starting to scare you?

689
00:39:48,303 --> 00:39:50,178
Are you finally afraid
you might get caught?

690
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:51,222
[scoffs]

691
00:39:51,598 --> 00:39:52,849
Unbelievable.

692
00:40:02,275 --> 00:40:03,568
[Seongwon] Everyone

693
00:40:04,819 --> 00:40:06,528
asks me why.

694
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:09,531
"Why? Why on earth?"

695
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:12,284
As if they could understand
if I told them.

696
00:40:12,285 --> 00:40:13,536
But the thing is,

697
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:17,790
there is no answer to begin with.

698
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:21,419
I am...

699
00:40:23,379 --> 00:40:26,924
beyond the understanding
of someone like you.

700
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:27,926
You're right.

701
00:40:30,553 --> 00:40:32,847
I treated you like a person,

702
00:40:33,765 --> 00:40:35,558
when you're not even human.

703
00:40:39,729 --> 00:40:41,564
I'm working on a new piece.

704
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:43,274
Would you like to see?

705
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:54,159
[♪ ominous sting plays]

706
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,578
[breath trembling]

707
00:40:58,373 --> 00:40:59,707
[♪ music fades]

708
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:05,004
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

709
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:10,050
Hey, I told you to stop coming.

710
00:41:10,051 --> 00:41:12,261
I wouldn't have to come
if you had a girlfriend.

711
00:41:13,346 --> 00:41:15,013
You didn't like the hospital food.

712
00:41:15,014 --> 00:41:18,643
Oh, I can't resist fried chicken.
[chuckles softly]

713
00:41:24,273 --> 00:41:25,316
[chuckles]

714
00:41:31,072 --> 00:41:32,323
Here.

715
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,998
Hey, I told you
not to look at me like that.

716
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:42,499
What do you mean? Like what?

717
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:45,544
It was my mistake that got me stabbed,

718
00:41:45,545 --> 00:41:46,587
so stop doing that.

719
00:41:48,423 --> 00:41:51,092
[inhales deeply]
Your mistake is my mistake, too.

720
00:41:51,884 --> 00:41:53,177
Seriously!

721
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:56,723
Fine, I'll stop.

722
00:41:57,306 --> 00:41:58,307
Just eat up.

723
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:00,643
[chuckles]

724
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:04,147
- Is it good?
- [both chuckle]

725
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:06,690
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

726
00:42:06,691 --> 00:42:08,109
[breath trembling]

727
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:16,492
[breathing shakily]

728
00:42:20,872 --> 00:42:22,874
Are you that touched?

729
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:25,460
[breathing shakily]

730
00:42:28,588 --> 00:42:29,714
[grunts]

731
00:42:29,839 --> 00:42:31,298
[Isoo] Detective Joo!

732
00:42:31,299 --> 00:42:32,424
[grunts]

733
00:42:32,425 --> 00:42:33,634
[Hyera crying]

734
00:42:40,683 --> 00:42:43,185
Jeez. Isoo!

735
00:42:43,186 --> 00:42:45,395
She's out of control right now.

736
00:42:45,396 --> 00:42:47,273
[Hyera panting, breath trembling]

737
00:42:49,776 --> 00:42:51,526
Are you going to trust someone like her?

738
00:42:51,527 --> 00:42:53,154
You shut your mouth.

739
00:42:57,784 --> 00:42:59,117
[scoffs, mutters]

740
00:42:59,118 --> 00:43:00,787
[breathing heavily]

741
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:11,881
[♪ music fades]

742
00:43:13,549 --> 00:43:15,801
It's possible he was murdered here.

743
00:43:15,802 --> 00:43:17,594
- We need to find traces of blood.
- [KCSI officers] Okay.

744
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:19,847
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

745
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:31,275
[camera shutter clicking]

746
00:43:46,541 --> 00:43:47,667
[♪ music fades]

747
00:43:52,296 --> 00:43:53,798
[line connects, ringing]

748
00:43:56,509 --> 00:43:58,469
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

749
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:00,470
[sighs softly]

750
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:02,473
- [sighs wearily]
- [cell phone vibrating]

751
00:44:07,603 --> 00:44:09,730
Yeah. Did you find anything?

752
00:44:09,856 --> 00:44:11,273
[Junyoung] <i>No.</i> [sighs]

753
00:44:11,274 --> 00:44:13,192
There's no trace of blood anywhere.

754
00:44:13,818 --> 00:44:15,653
This might not be where he was killed.

755
00:44:18,739 --> 00:44:19,949
[cell phone snaps shut]

756
00:44:28,291 --> 00:44:29,542
[line connects, ringing]

757
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:33,379
- [line clicks]
- Yes, Dr. Yoon.

758
00:44:34,714 --> 00:44:36,256
Did you look at the body?

759
00:44:36,257 --> 00:44:39,050
It looks like they used a stun gun.

760
00:44:39,051 --> 00:44:41,345
There's an indentation
in the back of his head,

761
00:44:42,305 --> 00:44:45,433
and there are bruises all over his body.

762
00:44:46,184 --> 00:44:47,560
[sighs deeply]

763
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:49,854
[exhales softly]

764
00:44:54,025 --> 00:44:55,234
Should I go in alone?

765
00:44:56,194 --> 00:44:57,320
[exhales]

766
00:44:57,820 --> 00:44:59,071
No, let's go together.

767
00:45:04,619 --> 00:45:05,786
[♪ music fades]

768
00:45:06,454 --> 00:45:08,663
At 11:00 p.m. on Sunday,

769
00:45:08,664 --> 00:45:10,249
you went to UBS's main office.

770
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:12,501
Why?

771
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:16,672
Tell us what you did after that.

772
00:45:17,173 --> 00:45:18,340
[sighs in exasperation]

773
00:45:18,341 --> 00:45:20,218
This is seriously no fun. [clicks tongue]

774
00:45:21,552 --> 00:45:23,303
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

775
00:45:23,304 --> 00:45:24,680
[breathes deeply]

776
00:45:26,349 --> 00:45:27,350
Isoo.

777
00:45:28,226 --> 00:45:29,644
What are you doing?

778
00:45:30,519 --> 00:45:32,563
Why do you keep pretending you're normal?

779
00:45:33,147 --> 00:45:35,148
Are you going to
keep asking dumb questions?

780
00:45:35,149 --> 00:45:37,276
How long do I have to keep
opening your eyes?

781
00:45:38,736 --> 00:45:39,737
Right.

782
00:45:41,864 --> 00:45:43,699
That's why you killed Younghwan.

783
00:45:44,784 --> 00:45:47,286
Because you thought we were alike.

784
00:45:49,372 --> 00:45:50,748
You said you grew up lonely.

785
00:45:51,624 --> 00:45:53,125
That you felt abandoned.

786
00:45:54,168 --> 00:45:56,921
You assumed we were the same
and got the wrong idea.

787
00:45:59,090 --> 00:46:00,091
I'm not like you.

788
00:46:02,051 --> 00:46:03,052
I had...

789
00:46:07,181 --> 00:46:09,140
a mother who cherished me.

790
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:10,643
[♪ music turns ominous]

791
00:46:12,812 --> 00:46:14,771
You didn't have a mother like that.

792
00:46:14,772 --> 00:46:17,191
That's why you ended up completely broken.

793
00:46:17,858 --> 00:46:19,568
You were damaged beyond repair.

794
00:46:22,571 --> 00:46:25,365
After Kim Younghwan died
and Cho Pilgu was caught,

795
00:46:25,366 --> 00:46:27,410
did you feel scared and run to your mom?

796
00:46:28,077 --> 00:46:29,744
Did you beg her for help?

797
00:46:29,745 --> 00:46:31,746
From the mom who despises you?

798
00:46:31,747 --> 00:46:33,249
[♪ music increases in tempo]

799
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:35,543
[scoffs softly]

800
00:46:38,212 --> 00:46:39,255
[♪ music fades]

801
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:52,518
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

802
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:04,864
Hey, isn't that Chairwoman Jeong Taeseon?

803
00:47:05,448 --> 00:47:06,573
I think it is.

804
00:47:06,574 --> 00:47:07,783
[♪ music swells]

805
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:11,787
[♪ music fades]

806
00:47:13,289 --> 00:47:16,792
We're looking for the man
who impersonated a lawyer.

807
00:47:17,710 --> 00:47:21,172
We're also combing through the place
where you disposed of the body.

808
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:24,090
We'll pull footage
from every camera nearby.

809
00:47:24,091 --> 00:47:26,134
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

810
00:47:26,135 --> 00:47:27,803
[sighs deeply]

811
00:47:31,849 --> 00:47:33,267
I'm going to catch you in the end.

812
00:47:35,770 --> 00:47:38,981
Save yourself the humiliation
of being dragged in and just confess.

813
00:47:39,690 --> 00:47:41,149
[sighs, scoffs]

814
00:47:41,150 --> 00:47:42,985
[laughing smugly]

815
00:47:44,195 --> 00:47:48,032
Why do you keep saying I killed someone?

816
00:47:49,033 --> 00:47:51,077
Why would I kill him?

817
00:47:51,702 --> 00:47:52,703
I mean,

818
00:47:53,913 --> 00:47:54,914
did he follow me...

819
00:47:58,084 --> 00:47:59,626
and spy on me or something?

820
00:47:59,627 --> 00:48:02,713
Because of his foolish superior
who thinks I'm a murderer?

821
00:48:06,342 --> 00:48:08,176
Unless that's what pissed me off,

822
00:48:08,177 --> 00:48:10,638
there's no reason for me to kill him.

823
00:48:14,100 --> 00:48:15,101
Oh.

824
00:48:15,935 --> 00:48:16,936
Right there.

825
00:48:17,937 --> 00:48:19,188
That's a great expression.

826
00:48:21,315 --> 00:48:22,316
Want to be my model?

827
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:26,695
[exhales sharply]

828
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:32,576
[♪ music fades]

829
00:48:33,953 --> 00:48:36,789
Mr. Yu Seongwon, please get up.

830
00:48:39,667 --> 00:48:41,167
[Seongwon sighs contentedly]

831
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:43,045
- Sir.
- Be quiet.

832
00:48:44,088 --> 00:48:45,172
[scoffs softly]

833
00:48:48,759 --> 00:48:50,845
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

834
00:49:20,082 --> 00:49:21,208
[door closes]

835
00:49:28,507 --> 00:49:29,674
[Hyera] Wait!

836
00:49:29,675 --> 00:49:30,926
[Hyera panting]

837
00:49:33,762 --> 00:49:35,055
Your son is a murderer.

838
00:49:38,726 --> 00:49:40,019
He killed five people.

839
00:49:47,610 --> 00:49:48,736
You know, don't you?

840
00:49:50,696 --> 00:49:51,697
You're his mother.

841
00:49:52,615 --> 00:49:53,866
Of course, you know.

842
00:49:56,076 --> 00:49:58,078
He's going to continue killing people.

843
00:49:59,288 --> 00:50:01,123
This isn't something you can cover up.

844
00:50:04,752 --> 00:50:06,045
You have no manners.

845
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:08,464
And have no fear.

846
00:50:09,548 --> 00:50:11,509
People like that
usually come to a bad end.

847
00:50:14,512 --> 00:50:15,763
You should be careful.

848
00:50:24,855 --> 00:50:25,856
[car door closes]

849
00:50:27,608 --> 00:50:28,859
[♪ music swells]

850
00:50:40,371 --> 00:50:41,538
[♪ music fades]

851
00:50:41,539 --> 00:50:43,832
Keep your subordinates in line!

852
00:50:44,500 --> 00:50:45,583
Yes, sir.

853
00:50:45,584 --> 00:50:47,086
For Christ's sake.

854
00:50:53,717 --> 00:50:55,344
From now on,

855
00:50:56,262 --> 00:50:57,720
this case goes to Team 2!

856
00:50:57,721 --> 00:50:59,847
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

857
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:01,599
- You can't.
- I can't?

858
00:51:01,600 --> 00:51:03,769
- I've been too patient with you.
- Sir.

859
00:51:07,398 --> 00:51:08,440
[scoffs softly]

860
00:51:09,733 --> 00:51:12,277
I heard the victim was
your junior officer.

861
00:51:12,278 --> 00:51:13,736
Huh?

862
00:51:13,737 --> 00:51:16,824
Can an involved party
be in charge of a case?

863
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:20,536
I'm the one

864
00:51:21,787 --> 00:51:23,247
who knows this case best.

865
00:51:24,582 --> 00:51:26,125
Yu Seongwon is the killer.

866
00:51:27,960 --> 00:51:29,085
Do you have evidence?

867
00:51:29,086 --> 00:51:30,296
I'm going to find it.

868
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:33,673
[scoffs] Isn't it all just in your head?

869
00:51:33,674 --> 00:51:37,135
You've invented a whole story,
and you're twisting everything to fit.

870
00:51:37,136 --> 00:51:38,137
No, I'm not.

871
00:51:39,013 --> 00:51:40,014
Yu Seongwon

872
00:51:41,098 --> 00:51:43,225
has been killing people continuously.

873
00:51:44,893 --> 00:51:48,605
You're out of your mind. [exclaims]

874
00:51:48,606 --> 00:51:50,607
Stay out of this investigation!

875
00:51:50,608 --> 00:51:52,401
- Sir.
- Chief Park.

876
00:51:53,319 --> 00:51:56,654
The body of Joo Hyera's junior officer
was delivered to her.

877
00:51:56,655 --> 00:52:01,452
Can she stay on this case?

878
00:52:05,914 --> 00:52:07,081
She can't.

879
00:52:07,082 --> 00:52:08,626
[♪ music increases in tempo]

880
00:52:15,466 --> 00:52:16,549
Team 2!

881
00:52:16,550 --> 00:52:18,676
Don't spin some story like she did.

882
00:52:18,677 --> 00:52:21,179
Find the real killer, got it?

883
00:52:21,180 --> 00:52:22,222
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

884
00:52:23,015 --> 00:52:25,059
Damn it.

885
00:52:27,394 --> 00:52:28,479
[door closes]

886
00:52:29,563 --> 00:52:30,731
[♪ music fades]

887
00:52:35,694 --> 00:52:37,029
Leave the country right now.

888
00:52:37,738 --> 00:52:39,238
I told you I have an exhibition.

889
00:52:39,239 --> 00:52:41,325
Must I really go through this
because of you?

890
00:52:46,497 --> 00:52:47,955
[inhales sharply]

891
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:51,335
I think we'll have to kill
that boyfriend of yours.

892
00:52:53,212 --> 00:52:54,797
- What?
- Why?

893
00:52:55,464 --> 00:52:56,465
Do you love him?

894
00:52:57,257 --> 00:52:58,341
[scoffs]

895
00:52:58,342 --> 00:53:00,134
You don't know anything about that.

896
00:53:00,135 --> 00:53:01,303
[sighs heavily]

897
00:53:04,640 --> 00:53:07,643
You had me because you wanted
to be the chairman's second wife.

898
00:53:08,852 --> 00:53:09,853
But

899
00:53:10,521 --> 00:53:12,022
even just a little,

900
00:53:14,692 --> 00:53:16,568
did you ever love me?

901
00:53:20,572 --> 00:53:22,699
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

902
00:53:22,700 --> 00:53:24,034
[breathes deeply]

903
00:53:24,993 --> 00:53:26,828
Isoo told me

904
00:53:26,829 --> 00:53:29,206
that I ended up broken because of you.

905
00:53:29,915 --> 00:53:31,541
So you should take responsibility.

906
00:53:31,542 --> 00:53:33,167
Leave the country for a while.

907
00:53:33,168 --> 00:53:35,086
The police have nothing on me.

908
00:53:35,087 --> 00:53:36,838
They don't have any evidence.

909
00:53:36,839 --> 00:53:39,007
Stay away until things settle down!

910
00:53:41,635 --> 00:53:42,928
[swears softly]

911
00:53:45,889 --> 00:53:48,726
Should I just come clean?

912
00:53:50,144 --> 00:53:53,397
Seeing you with your head down
and your hands cuffed,

913
00:53:53,981 --> 00:53:57,900
being dragged around,
while reporters take pictures of you...

914
00:53:57,901 --> 00:54:00,821
[laughing] ...might actually be quite fun.

915
00:54:03,490 --> 00:54:05,367
- Honestly.
- [♪ music fades]

916
00:54:06,201 --> 00:54:08,953
What do you mean
Yu Seongwon has been killing people?

917
00:54:08,954 --> 00:54:10,831
Are you saying he's a serial killer?

918
00:54:11,874 --> 00:54:12,957
Yes.

919
00:54:12,958 --> 00:54:14,333
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

920
00:54:14,334 --> 00:54:15,753
Two of Yu Seongwon's models

921
00:54:16,545 --> 00:54:18,255
and his underclassman are missing.

922
00:54:19,089 --> 00:54:20,215
Detective Joo thinks

923
00:54:21,049 --> 00:54:25,178
Yu Seongwon was inspired by his murders
and created these pieces.

924
00:54:25,179 --> 00:54:27,473
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

925
00:54:29,308 --> 00:54:32,519
After Kim Heejun went missing,
Yu Seongwon left for the UK.

926
00:54:33,187 --> 00:54:34,980
He came back recently for an exhibition.

927
00:54:36,106 --> 00:54:37,608
Detective Joo moved back here

928
00:54:38,734 --> 00:54:40,068
to catch Yu Seongwon.

929
00:54:41,153 --> 00:54:42,488
To catch Yu Seongwon?

930
00:54:43,197 --> 00:54:45,491
Then what happened to Jeong Minjae?

931
00:54:46,492 --> 00:54:49,995
He was following Yu Seongwon,
and then we lost contact with him.

932
00:54:52,623 --> 00:54:53,998
[sighs deeply]

933
00:54:53,999 --> 00:54:56,250
Do you think
Yu Seongwon is the killer, too?

934
00:54:56,251 --> 00:54:58,587
Yes, I'm certain.

935
00:55:00,464 --> 00:55:02,925
He killed Younghwan to provoke me.

936
00:55:05,511 --> 00:55:07,638
But we don't have any evidence.

937
00:55:08,263 --> 00:55:09,431
[♪ music fades]

938
00:55:10,015 --> 00:55:11,474
These are old case files.

939
00:55:11,475 --> 00:55:13,809
Let's check them
to see if we've missed anything.

940
00:55:13,810 --> 00:55:15,311
- Okay.
- [sighs]

941
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:17,022
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

942
00:55:19,149 --> 00:55:20,400
[sighs in exasperation]

943
00:55:20,984 --> 00:55:23,152
[sniffles, sighs heavily]

944
00:55:23,153 --> 00:55:25,280
[breath trembling, sighing]

945
00:55:28,158 --> 00:55:29,242
Hyera.

946
00:55:29,243 --> 00:55:30,827
[Hyera sniffles, sighs]

947
00:55:32,120 --> 00:55:33,539
[exhales softly]

948
00:55:37,084 --> 00:55:38,292
I know how you feel.

949
00:55:38,293 --> 00:55:39,795
[breath trembling]

950
00:55:41,004 --> 00:55:42,464
[Changun]
Just pull yourself together first.

951
00:55:45,050 --> 00:55:46,468
We're going to catch Yu Seongwon.

952
00:55:47,219 --> 00:55:48,512
It may seem hopeless right now,

953
00:55:50,097 --> 00:55:51,681
but we'll catch him in the end.

954
00:55:51,682 --> 00:55:53,392
[breath continues trembling]

955
00:55:55,602 --> 00:55:56,937
[♪ music swells]

956
00:56:01,233 --> 00:56:02,442
[♪ music fades]

957
00:56:04,653 --> 00:56:06,363
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

958
00:56:11,910 --> 00:56:13,703
[Isoo] <i>You didn't have a mother like that.</i>

959
00:56:13,704 --> 00:56:15,747
That's why you ended up completely broken.

960
00:56:17,082 --> 00:56:18,874
You were damaged beyond repair.

961
00:56:18,875 --> 00:56:20,961
Did you feel scared and run to your mom?

962
00:56:22,254 --> 00:56:24,005
Did you beg her for help?

963
00:56:24,006 --> 00:56:25,924
From the mom who despises you?

964
00:56:26,508 --> 00:56:27,551
[sighs softly]

965
00:56:28,635 --> 00:56:29,720
[scoffs]

966
00:56:30,762 --> 00:56:32,014
[sighs wearily]

967
00:56:34,433 --> 00:56:35,809
[sighs deeply]

968
00:56:39,438 --> 00:56:40,814
[shattering]

969
00:56:41,523 --> 00:56:42,983
[breathing heavily]

970
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:46,445
[clangs]

971
00:56:49,906 --> 00:56:51,658
[hurried footsteps approaching]

972
00:56:57,456 --> 00:56:58,624
[sighs softly]

973
00:57:05,589 --> 00:57:06,797
[groans softly]

974
00:57:06,798 --> 00:57:08,050
[♪ music increases in tempo]

975
00:57:08,634 --> 00:57:09,801
[inhales deeply]

976
00:57:12,804 --> 00:57:14,221
[exhales deeply]

977
00:57:14,222 --> 00:57:15,515
[♪ music swells]

978
00:57:21,229 --> 00:57:22,314
[sighs softly]

979
00:57:24,816 --> 00:57:25,941
[♪ music fades]

980
00:57:25,942 --> 00:57:28,611
TWO DAYS EARLIER

981
00:57:28,612 --> 00:57:30,530
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

982
00:57:40,582 --> 00:57:41,707
[scoffs]

983
00:57:41,708 --> 00:57:43,043
[♪ music increases in tempo]

984
00:58:45,105 --> 00:58:46,398
[♪ music swells]

985
00:58:47,524 --> 00:58:49,025
- [taser crackling]
- [heavy thud]

986
00:58:49,735 --> 00:58:51,111
[♪ music resumes tempo]

987
00:58:55,615 --> 00:58:57,826
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

988
00:59:37,699 --> 00:59:41,453
[♪ ominous chord swells]

989
00:59:43,872 --> 00:59:45,331
[chuckles softly]

990
00:59:45,332 --> 00:59:47,459
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

991
00:59:49,336 --> 00:59:50,462
[Mr. Hwang grunts]

992
00:59:58,762 --> 01:00:00,472
[flames roaring]

993
01:00:12,943 --> 01:00:14,486
[♪ music swells]

994
01:00:31,670 --> 01:00:32,754
[inhales sharply]

995
01:00:34,548 --> 01:00:35,674
[exhales deeply]

996
01:00:36,967 --> 01:00:38,009
[chuckles softly]

997
01:00:45,892 --> 01:00:47,060
[laughs maliciously]

998
01:00:54,651 --> 01:00:55,776
[♪ music fades]

999
01:00:55,777 --> 01:00:56,861
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 12

1000
01:00:56,862 --> 01:00:58,362
THE MADNESS IS FINALLY UNVEILED

1001
01:00:58,363 --> 01:00:59,823
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1002
01:01:33,398 --> 01:01:35,149
What's Yu Seongwon's weakness?

1003
01:01:35,150 --> 01:01:36,317
Don't touch my son.

1004
01:01:36,318 --> 01:01:37,735
[Taegyun] <i>You're suspended as of now.</i>

1005
01:01:37,736 --> 01:01:38,903
[Isoo] <i>I'll resign.</i>

1006
01:01:38,904 --> 01:01:40,112
[Hyera] Jin Isoo!

1007
01:01:40,113 --> 01:01:42,072
[Isoo] <i>Detective Joo,
stay and hold the line.</i>

1008
01:01:42,073 --> 01:01:44,825
Hello! Watch how far I can go.

1009
01:01:44,826 --> 01:01:46,243
<i>They're even threatening to sue.</i>

1010
01:01:46,244 --> 01:01:47,912
I have a plane ready. Get out now.

1011
01:01:47,913 --> 01:01:49,622
Yu Seongwon's flying out in two hours.

1012
01:01:49,623 --> 01:01:50,789
<i>Just go and arrest him first.</i>

1013
01:01:50,790 --> 01:01:53,500
Now's the time to repay your debt.

1014
01:01:53,501 --> 01:01:55,337
- [tires screech]
- [Kyungjin] Pull over!

1015
01:01:56,004 --> 01:01:57,505
[man] <i>Jin Isoo is in the studio.</i>

1016
01:01:58,214 --> 01:01:59,299
Burn them all.

1017
01:02:00,717 --> 01:02:03,762
[Seongwon] <i>Do you really think
you can catch me?</i>

1018
01:02:06,973 --> 01:02:08,141
[♪ music fades]

1019
01:02:13,146 --> 01:02:14,605
[woman] <i>Mr. Yu, welcome.</i>

1020
01:02:14,606 --> 01:02:16,523
Hello.

1021
01:02:16,524 --> 01:02:19,485
Looking handsome as always.
How have you been?

1022
01:02:19,486 --> 01:02:21,237
Doing well. How about you, Director?

1023
01:02:21,821 --> 01:02:24,281
It's been frantic getting ready
for the exhibition.

1024
01:02:24,282 --> 01:02:26,284
This way, please.
I have the pieces all set up.

1025
01:02:34,626 --> 01:02:35,710
What do you think?

1026
01:02:38,588 --> 01:02:40,340
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

1027
01:02:42,092 --> 01:02:43,468
As for this exhibition...

1028
01:02:48,223 --> 01:02:49,891
That one is the centerpiece.

1029
01:02:52,602 --> 01:02:56,106
It should be the first thing people see
when they walk in.

1030
01:02:59,150 --> 01:03:02,237
It needs to feel real...

1031
01:03:03,029 --> 01:03:04,948
as if it were alive.

1032
01:03:07,367 --> 01:03:08,701
Understood?

1033
01:03:08,702 --> 01:03:10,704
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
